<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
  CoreDiverging: 64 entry diverging colormap for VTL, VTU, and CPSidx
  (cyclone core structure fields, see D2D/README.md). Negative values
  are cold core and read blue; positive values are warm core and read
  red. CAVE stretches these 64 entries evenly across whichever
  styleRule range references this file (e.g. +/-2.0e-4 for VTL/VTU,
  -3 to 3 for CPSidx), so index 0 is always the coldest/most negative
  end and index 63 the warmest/most positive end regardless of the
  physical units involved.

  The middle 8 entries (indices 28 through 35) are fully transparent
  (a="0.0") on purpose: values near zero are the cold/warm-core
  boundary, not a meaningful magnitude, and painting them as an opaque
  fill would hide MSLP contours plotted underneath in the same panel.
  Alpha ramps from 0.0 at the edge of that transparent band up to 1.0
  over the next 6 entries on each side (indices 22-27 and 36-41) so the
  fill fades in gradually instead of snapping from invisible to solid
  at the band edge. Everything outside indices 22-41 is fully opaque.

  File format: a root <colorMap> element containing an ordered list of
  <color r="" g="" b="" a=""/> entries, each component a float from
  0.0 to 1.0, in index order from index 0 (first <color>) to the last.
  This follows the AWIPS/CAVE ColorMap XML schema documented for
  gridded imagery colormaps; no .cmap file existed anywhere in this
  repo or on this machine to check by example, so VERIFY the element
  name ("colorMap") and attribute names (r, g, b, a) against an actual
  .cmap file under your site's or the base build's
  common_static/.../colormaps directory before installing this, since
  the schema can drift between AWIPS versions.
-->
<colorMap>
        <color r="0.050" g="0.150" b="0.600" a="1.0"/>
        <color r="0.060" g="0.165" b="0.615" a="1.0"/>
        <color r="0.070" g="0.180" b="0.630" a="1.0"/>
